          "passage": "Surveys of U.S. adult social media use, conducted by the Pew Research Center over the course of the 2010s, allow researchers to compare growth trajectories across the major platforms in roughly the same population over time. A media-studies student summarizing Pew's published time-series data argues that the trajectory of Facebook use is best characterized as a sharp expansion in the early 2010s followed by a near-plateau, distinct from the steadier growth seen at platforms with smaller user bases. The student supports the claim with data from the table.",
