          "skill": "command-of-evidence-textual",
          "passage": "The geobiologist Hope Jahren has argued, in her writing about her own laboratory practice, that the technical demands of stable-isotope work on fossil plants — measuring the carbon and oxygen ratios locked into ancient wood and seeds — set limits on what climate-history questions a single project can usefully address. A literary critic argues that this argument runs through her 2016 memoir *Lab Girl* not as an abstract methodological claim but as a recurring practical theme: the day-to-day texture of choosing instruments, sample sizes, and replicate counts shapes which questions a research group can actually take on, often more than the broader theoretical interest of a question does.",
