          "band": 3,
          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "command-of-evidence-textual",
          "passage": "Robert Louis Stevenson's 1886 novel *Kidnapped* is told in the first person by David Balfour, a young Lowland Scot who, after escaping the brig that has carried him toward the colonies, falls in with the Highland Jacobite Alan Breck Stewart on the journey south. A literary critic argues that Stevenson uses David's narration not to settle whether Highland or Lowland readers are correctly placed in the political quarrel of the period but to dramatize how thoroughly David's own categories shift, even within a single conversation, once Alan begins to speak.",
