          "passage": "In a series of careful experiments at the Marine Biological Laboratory at Woods Hole and at Columbia University in the 1940s, the geneticist Barbara McClintock showed that segments of maize chromosomes can change their position within the genome. The pattern of broken and rejoined chromosomes she observed across successive plant generations ______ the controlling-element framework she would defend, against considerable initial skepticism, for the rest of her career.",
