          "passage": "Atmospheric scientist Warren Washington spent five decades at the National Center for Atmospheric Research building general circulation models that simulate the coupled behavior of the atmosphere and ocean. In a 2007 essay reflecting on the modeling enterprise, Washington argued that the value of such models lies less in any single forecast they produce and more in the ______ they impose on the modeling team: every assumption, every parameterization, every choice of grid resolution must be stated explicitly, defended, and revisited as new observations come in.",
