          "passage": "Frances Ellen Watkins Harper's 1892 novel *Iola Leroy* follows a young woman of mixed parentage from her childhood in a Mississippi household — where she has been raised as white, in ignorance of her mother's enslaved background — through emancipation, separation from her family, and a postwar career as a teacher in the South. A literary critic argues that Harper uses the novel's late chapters not to settle the question of whether reunion with her surviving family is achievable for the title character but to dramatize the deliberate choices of vocational labor that organize her postwar adult life, with the recovered family ties depicted as supportive of, rather than substituting for, that labor.",
